WHY THIS SHAPE (read first): five candidates in this batch failed on claude-opus-5 (AGENTS.md §2, newest bullets: "Additive repair disarms a keep-today trap", "Evidence-reconstruction shape collapses once the panel makes it complete"). Every time, once the contract was unambiguous enough to pass review, both solvers wrote their own reference from the text, fuzzed it and solved. The design lever here: a small synthesizable Verilog module (iverilog + yosys in a digest-pinned Debian bookworm image) with a numbered, complete, unambiguous per-cycle spec (a register/port timing document with cycle diagrams in ASCII), whose difficulty is SAME-CYCLE INTERACTION of several well-defined rules (e.g. back-pressure deasserting in the cycle a descriptor completes, a credit returned in the cycle it is consumed, a flush arriving with a pending grant, counter wrap coinciding with a reload). These are fully specified, so fair, but a solver's own self-check is a testbench written from the same reading, which tends to share its blind spots on simultaneity; the hidden verifier is a cycle-accurate reference model driving constrained-random stimulus that concentrates such coincidences and compares every port every cycle. Either (a) a repair task: shipped RTL with 5–8 seeded per-cycle departures and correct-but-ugly corners that the natural rewrite breaks, or (b) a from-spec implementation of one small block with a stub. Pick whichever gives the stronger same-cycle interaction; keep the RTL under ~300 lines and the spec ~2 pages.

Read first, completely: AGENTS.md §1 and §2 (incl. the RTL bullet in §8 about hierarchical reads/$fopen lint and demotion); .agent/skills/task-batch/references/execution-profiles.md; .agent/skills/terminus-regular-task-authoring/SKILL.md and references bounded-task-design.md, contract-closure.md (§1–14 fairness), scaffold-five-axis-checklist.md, platform-checks.md, panel-precheck.md; task-miner/solver_path_screen.md and category_rules.md; skim task-local-solve-probe SKILL. For harness mechanics only, look at workspace/tasks/tbrain-workers-comp-disability-benefit (and tbrain-link-replay-transmitter if present anywhere, for RTL lint/demotion ideas only).

